<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36241" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντήκω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pour in while molten,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόλιβδον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					2.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. μόλιβδον [τῇ κεφαλῇ]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>CG</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τέτανον τερπνόν</span>
			v. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				553
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, with pf.
			
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντέτηκα,</span>
			<i>to be dissolved in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδατι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aët.
					9.42
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be cast,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδριάντα χαλκῷ ἐντετηκότα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.Chr.
					64.4
				</span></i>
			: but usu., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			metaph., of feelings, <i>sink deep in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῖσος ἐντέτηκέ μοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1311
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Mx.</u>
				245d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δέος ἐντετηκὸς ταῖς ψυχαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					6.72
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς ψυχαῖς ἐντέτηκεν ἡ
					δεισιδαιμονία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.83
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντήκεται γὰρ πλευμόνων ὅσοις
				ἔνι ψυχή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπρις</span>) <i>sinks in</i> . . as the breath of life,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				941.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of persons,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἂν εἰ κάρτ᾽ ἐντακείη τῷ
				φιλεῖν</span>
			<i>should be absorbed by</i> love, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				463
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρήνοισιν ἐντακεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					498
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
